Z||000001||fierohoho||10-24-2001||10:32 AM||||I'm not sure how much but the swap is pretty straight forward.<P>No cutting involved, it's all pretty much bolt in stuff.<P>Whoever does it will need the shifter and cables, transmission with flywheel,clutch and slave cylinder, maybe axels(not sure), the pedal assembly from a clutch car along with the clutch master cylider and the hydraulic line to connect the master and slave.<P>Don't forget the manual tranny console cover for the interior.<P>From this list you can see it could be quite expensive.<P>Can I ask why you want to do the swap?<P>Might be cheaper to look for a stick car to replace your auto.<P>------------------<BR>'84 SE 2.5l<BR>'85 Coupe 2.5l now getting a 3800<BR>'86 SE 2.5l<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/lightbar.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by fierohoho (edited 10-24-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||isthiswhereiputausername?||10-24-2001||11:22 AM||||like fierohoho said, it would be a lot of work..<P><BR>you would need the axles also with it,<P>if you could locate a parts car and swap everything over might be the easiest..<P>list:<P>tranny<BR>shift & select cables <BR>axles<BR>shifter console <BR>clutch master cyl<BR>clutch pedal<P><BR>I have everything on my parts car (listed in mall)needed to swap it for you, but shipping would be crazy on the tranny & axles..<P>if you can locate a tranny & axles out of a mid 80's fwd car (they will fit)  I can hook you up with the cables,shift console,clutch cyl & pedal <P><BR>||||reg||1
